<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Are-Ona-Kakanfo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Are-Ona-Kakanfo was the title of the supreme field commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>'s army. The holder was expected to be victorious in war and was traditionally stationed away from the capital. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonja">Afonja</a>, holder of the office at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilorin">Ilorin</a>, rebelled against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaafin">Alaafin</a> in the early nineteenth century, it contributed decisively to Oyo's collapse.</p></div>
